        <body>
            <div xml:id="d429">

                <pb facs="0417" n="335" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg335"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 895.52/4.</note>
                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-04-08"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 8,
                    1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to recent correspondence
                    concerning the land-investigation law of Chosen, I have the honor to transmit
                    herewith copies of self-explanatory letters, dated March 20 and April 4, as
                    received from the consul general at Seoul.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>(For <signed>Mr. O’Brien</signed>.)<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Montgomery Schuyler.</hi></signed></closer>




